            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0554" n="544" sameAs="frus:frus1942China/pg544"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7640: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-11-12T17:00:00-04:00">November 12,
                            1942—5 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1068. For Adler from the Secretary of the Treasury. Your 1147, October 8, 9 a.m.,
                    TF–63. Treasury does not object to the Board’s granting U. S. dollar exchange
                    for commercial imports from Russia. However, the Treasury would like to be
                    informed of the probable magnitude of exchange needed for such purposes.
                    [Morgenthau.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
